@startuml creator-identity-conflict-sequence
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
title Figure 4.3.4.2.4 View Creator Identity Conflicts Sequence Diagram
hide footbox
autonumber
actor "Data Manager" as Manager
participant "Web Client" as Web
participant AdminIdentityConflictController as API
participant CreatorIdentityConflictService as Service
participant CreatorIdentityConflictRepository as Repo
Manager -> Web : open identity conflicts
Web -> API : GET /api/v1/data/creator-conflicts
activate API
alt <U+005B>missing both REVIEW_CREATOR_CLAIM and RESOLVE_CREATOR_DUPLICATE (BR-70)<U+005D>
  API --> Web : access denied
else <U+005B>either authority granted<U+005D>
  API -> Service : listConflicts(status, pageable)
  activate Service
  alt <U+005B>status provided<U+005D>
    Service -> Repo : findByStatus(uppercaseStatus, pageable)
  else <U+005B>no status filter<U+005D>
    Service -> Repo : findAll(pageable)
  end
  Repo --> Service : matching conflict page
  Service --> API : page of ConflictDetailDto
  deactivate Service
  API --> Web : 200 OK
end
deactivate API
note over API, Service
  The controller exposes the list as GET. Ownership-transfer
  resolution has no HTTP mapping and the service rejects transfers.
end note
@enduml
